{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"agent_message","text":"The system switches from the heat pump to the natural gas furnace at an outdoor temperature of **35°F (about 1.7°C)**. The furnace supplies all heating at that temperature and below.\n\nSource: [*ResStock Measure Documentation: Dual Fuel Heat Pump*, Section 1.2.1.5, p. 5](https://docs.nlr.gov/docs/fy26osti/96414.pdf#page=13), which explicitly sets the upgrade’s switchover temperature at 35°F."}}
